Still working on my first coffee of the day, but my initial thought is that it may be related to the propagation of bias in the observation process on N through time. In other words, if both the dynamic and static models estimate an equally biased (low) detection probability, the realized estimate of N in the static model for each occasion will only be biased as a function of the biased detection rate for that occasion, but in the dynamic model, it will be biased as a function of each biased detection probability that occurred prior to that occasion as each estimate of N for each occasion will not only be biased, but will innately bias the estimate of N for the following time step.

