Could it be the priors distribution for the intrinsic growth rate? r0  is treated as the intrinsic growth rate in your model, but it seems heavily skewed towards some really large positive values. The prior seems more realistic too, if it's the finite growth rate instead. It still favors more positive values for growth, or was this by design?

sd0<-runif(100000,0,5)
mu0<-runif(100000,-2,2)

r0<-rnorm(mu0,sd0)

plot(density(exp(r0)), xlim=c(-50,500))#prior density if r0 is intrinsic growth
plot(density(r0))#prior density if r0 is finite growth

median(r0)
median(exp(r0))

