For what it's worth, when I included density-dependence with the Gompertz form (log(N[i,k] + 1) this seemed to exacerbate the population increases with time. However, holding p constant over the study period but still retaining the Gompertz D-D gave estimates more consistent with the observed counts (attached). Perhaps there are issues with detectability and population growth covariates (or lack of relevant covariates)?

Adrian

